     "'(REMOVED)' is a SIXTH support state: support that once existed and was deliberately taken out. Distinct from 'never implemented' and from 'implemented but disabled' (nostr-rs-relay).",
     "Like nostr-rs-relay it claims NIP-12/15/16/20/33, all merged into NIP-01 and deleted.",
     "A separate README section is headed 'NIP-43 invite codes'. NIP-43 is not 'invite codes' in the registry (Amethyst calls it 'Relay Access Metadata and Requests'). Same number, third meaning."
